---
kind: lore
id: south.pebbletonTown
title: Pebbleton — services, the east road, and its people
---

// ── Monster Center and Mart ──────────────────────────────────────────────

<beat id="center" on="heal" target="town.pebbleton" title="Monster Center" once="false">
  ::use{component="nurse" town="pebbleton"}
</beat>

<beat id="mart" on="shop" target="town.pebbleton" title="Mart" once="false">
  ::use{component="shop" stock="pebbletonStock"}
</beat>

// the Center board's delivery (quests/south/side.lute southParcel): the
// clerk hands it over after the sale
<beat id="parcel" on="shop" target="town.pebbleton" title="The parcel for Granny Wren" also when="quest.southParcel.state == 'active'">
  @clerk: Oh! You're the one from the board? The Hollowtown parcel. It's seeds, I think. It rattles. Mind it in the wood.
  @narrator: {{userName}} took the parcel for Granny Wren.
</beat>

// ── The town, by slot (the first visit is south.pebbleton) ──────────────

<entry id="southPebbletonMorning" on="enterTown" target="town.pebbleton" category="bark" once="day" when="@isMorning">
  @narrator: Morning in Pebbleton: the miners going up the hill with their lamps unlit, the Stone Gym's doors already open.
</entry>

<entry id="southPebbletonDay" on="enterTown" target="town.pebbleton" category="bark" once="day" when="run.slot == 'day'">
  @narrator: Somebody in Pebbleton is always hammering something. Today it is the museum's red door, which somebody else keeps painting grey.
</entry>

<entry id="southPebbletonNight" on="enterTown" target="town.pebbleton" category="bark" once="day" when="@isNight">
  @narrator: At night the whole grey town turns silver, and you can see the moonlight on the mountain where the cave mouth is.
</entry>

// ── The east road (gate pebbletonEast opens with the Stone Badge) ────────

<entry id="southPebbletonEastShut" on="obstacle" target="gate.pebbletonEast" category="bark" when="!holds(canPass(pebbletonEast))">
  @pebbletonDobbs: Hold it. East road's for trainers who've seen Petra. Not beaten, necessarily. Seen. Well. Beaten. That's the rule.
</entry>

<entry id="southDobbsShut" on="talk" target="npc.pebbletonDobbs" category="bark" when="!holds(canPass(pebbletonEast))">
  @pebbletonDobbs: Nobody goes east without the Stone Badge. That boy Kai tried to tell me he had it in his other trousers.
</entry>

<entry id="southDobbsOpen" on="talk" target="npc.pebbletonDobbs" category="bark" priority="5" when="holds(canPass(pebbletonEast))">
  @pebbletonDobbs: The Stone Badge! Go on through, then. Moonstone Cave's up the ridge. Mind the Eclipse lot, if they're still there.
</entry>

// ── Curator Ottoline and Dr. Kell (museum) ──────────────────────────────

<entry id="southCuratorDone" on="talk" target="npc.pebbletonCurator" category="bark" priority="5" when="quest.southFossil.state == 'complete'">
  @pebbletonCurator{emotion="happy"}: A living fossil walked out of my back room! On legs! I've had to write a whole new placard.
</entry>

<entry id="southCurator" on="talk" target="npc.pebbletonCurator" category="bark">
  @pebbletonCurator: The wing fossil came out of the cliffs at Tidewell Cape, a hundred years ago. There are more in the cliffs, I'm sure of it. And more in Moonstone, if Eclipse leaves any.
</entry>

<entry id="southKellWaiting" on="talk" target="npc.pebbletonKell" category="bark" when="run.southFossil == 'none'">
  @pebbletonKell: Moonstone. Deep beds. Dome or spiral. Bring me one and I'll show you something your grandchildren won't believe.
</entry>

<entry id="southKellRest" on="talk" target="npc.pebbletonKell" category="bark" priority="-5" when="!visited('south.museumWing')">
  @pebbletonKell: The machine needs a rest. So do I. Come back when you've got both Southshore badges; the curator and I have an argument to finish.
</entry>

<entry id="southKellDone" on="talk" target="npc.pebbletonKell" category="bark" priority="-5" when="visited('south.museumWing')">
  @pebbletonKell{emotion="happy"}: Three revivals in one lifetime. My old professor managed one, and he fainted. Go and show them the sea.
</entry>

// ── Old Brask, the miner ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

<entry id="southBraskMorning" on="talk" target="npc.pebbletonBrask" category="bark" priority="10" when="@isMorning">
  @pebbletonBrask: Morning. Going up to the cave? Take a lamp. Take two. The dark in Moonstone eats lamps.
</entry>

<entry id="southBraskNight" on="talk" target="npc.pebbletonBrask" category="bark" priority="10" when="@isNight && run.lair.quarryDig != 'cleared'">
  @pebbletonBrask: Hear that? Picks. At this hour. Forty years I worked that mountain and I never once worked it at night.
</entry>

<entry id="southBrask" on="talk" target="npc.pebbletonBrask" category="bark">
  <match on="run.lair.quarryDig">
    <when is="cleared">
      @pebbletonBrask: You ran them off? The lot in black? Then I'll buy you a lemonade, and I'll tell everyone I'd have done it myself if my knees were younger.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @pebbletonBrask: Somebody's cut new steps into the deep workings. Neat steps. Not miners' steps. Miners cut steps like they're angry at the stairs.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</entry>

// ── Juniper, Petra's biggest fan ─────────────────────────────────────────

<entry id="southJuniperNight" on="talk" target="npc.pebbletonJuniper" category="bark" priority="10" when="@isNight">
  @pebbletonJuniper: Petra trains on the ridge at night, where nobody watches. Except me. I watch. From a respectful distance.
</entry>

<entry id="southJuniper" on="talk" target="npc.pebbletonJuniper" category="bark">
  <match>
    <when test="@badgeCount >= 1">
      @pebbletonJuniper{emotion="sad"}: You beat her. I'm happy for you. I'm devastated. I'm both. Petra says both is allowed.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @pebbletonJuniper: Petra's first monster was a Pebblet she found in a boot. She still has the boot.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</entry>
